#
#    AnimusForge.Curriculum.Interact.*
#        The interact stage (move3_interact, InteractEncounter): in an empty Deadmines, the object the goal names by its
#        kind (never its place) among DecoysMin to DecoysMax decoys of other kinds, behind a door whose lever opens it,
#        or the lock its key item opens (the cannon and the Defias Gunpowder the seat carries from the start). Arrive
#        (Outcome) is paid once, on the right object reached (stopped within 3 yd, within ArriveRise yards of its
#        height) or, for a lock, its key item used on it; DoorOpened (Outcome) once, the door opened by the seat's own
#        press on its lever. WrongObject (Cost) once a decoy, stopped beside or pressed; a refused press is priced as
#        Actions.Aimless.ActRefused. StepCost (per 50 ms), Death, Stuck, Wall and WallSlide as Seek's, the noise
#        prices fixed from the first step. Sighting (Shaping, faded) once, on the first frame listing the named object.
#        The ladder follows the fade's rungs (1, 0.5, 0): distinguish, switch, key; each rung keeps CarryShare of the
#        one below, its episodes RungSeconds0 to 2. Distinguish objects stand SightNearest to SightFurthest yards off
#        in sight of the seat, Spacing yards apart (Attempts draws). Summoned creatures within SummonSweep yards of a
#        site's opener (the cannon's pirates) are sent away at each reset.
AnimusForge.Curriculum.Interact.Arrive = 3.0
AnimusForge.Curriculum.Interact.DoorOpened = 1.0
AnimusForge.Curriculum.Interact.WrongObject = 0.5
AnimusForge.Curriculum.Interact.StepCost = 0.0005
